    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d735">

                <pb facs="0819" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/3133: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in
                    France</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-17T18:00:00-04:00">September 17, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>B–25. Your 106, September 14, noon, and your 111, September 17, 3 p.m.<anchor
                        n="43" xml:id="d735-f1"/> You may attend this meeting as an observer. Please
                    keep <pb facs="0820" n="721" xml:id="pg721"/> me informed of developments.
                    Beyond this I have no instructions at this time.</p>
                <p>Your work has been valuable and helpful and the Embassy at Madrid is at present
                    adequately staffed. Given the present situation at Madrid I do not believe that
                    it would be desirable for you or any other members of the staff to return there
                    at this time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d735-f1" n="43" xml:id="d735-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed; it reported that a meeting of the Diplomatic Corps would be
                    held Friday at 6 p.m., and requested instructions (852.00/3180).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
